# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env.
#
# There is no mock-data mode any more. EXPO_PUBLIC_USE_SUPABASE used to switch
# it, and this file used to tell you to leave it at 0 — but `USE_SUPABASE` is a
# hardcoded `true` in src/lib/config.ts, nothing reads the variable, and
# following the old instruction got you a `supabaseUrl is required` crash on
# launch. The two Supabase values below are required, not optional.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key
EXPO_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_live_or_test_xxx
# Server-side only (edge functions) — do NOT prefix with EXPO_PUBLIC:
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_or_test_xxx

# ── Posting a card straight to Instagram (optional) ─────────────────────────
#
# Without these the Share Kit still works: it composes the card and hands it to
# the phone's share sheet, which posts to the same account in two taps. What
# they add is the one-tap path, and both halves come from ONE Meta app:
#
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_INSTAGRAM_CLIENT_ID   the Meta app id. Public by design — it is
#                                     in the consent URL every coach sees.
#   INSTAGRAM_CLIENT_ID               the same value, as a SUPABASE SECRET, for
#                                     supabase/functions/instagram-publish.
#   INSTAGRAM_CLIENT_SECRET           the Meta app secret. A Supabase secret and
#                                     nothing else. It is never in the bundle.
#
# The Meta app also needs https://www.repplefitness.com/ads/callback listed
# under Valid OAuth Redirect URIs (the same page the ad-account sign-in uses),
# and instagram_content_publish approved through Meta App Review. Until that
# approval lands the screen says "not available" in those words.
EXPO_PUBLIC_INSTAGRAM_CLIENT_ID=
